Package: pubsubr
Type: Package
Title: Serverless Publish-Subscribe Interprocess Messaging
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jean-Philippe", "Gravel", email = "jeanphilippe.gravel@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Aaron", "Jacobs", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the 'sigterm' package, from which src/sigterm.c is adapted")
    )
Description: A serverless publish-subscribe library for local interprocess
    communication, with no broker or server process. Supports wildcard topics
    and graceful shutdown on termination signals. Messages are compatible with
    the Python 'formix-pubsub' library, so R and Python processes can exchange
    them.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Copyright: See inst/COPYRIGHTS. src/sigterm.c is adapted from the 'sigterm'
    package, Copyright Aaron Jacobs, under the Apache License 2.0.
URL: https://github.com/formix/pubsubr, https://github.com/formix/pubsub
BugReports: https://github.com/formix/pubsubr/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    logger,
    tools
Suggests:
    covr,
    parallel,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
OS_type: unix
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
